":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/9007","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/9007","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/9007.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/9007.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-13T00:45:08Z"},"body":"## Summary\n\n```diff\nPetnames::open\n  replay complete journal record\n+ normalize the name and reject normalization failures\n+ reject per-owner fold and skeleton duplicates\n  preserve torn-final-line handling\n```\n\nThe alleged-name skeleton check remains a load-time exemption because `open` has no directory state.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** replay applied `Set` records verbatim, bypassing `set()` validation (confirmed in the existing triage on #5225).\n- **After:** added fail-loud validation with journal line and invariant in the error, plus tests for fold duplicates, format characters, overlong names, skeleton duplicates, and a valid `set()` journal round-trip. `cargo test --manifest-path pkgs/id/Cargo.toml -p id-core petname` — **32 passed, 0 failed**. PR CI was queued/in progress at the last check.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** narrow — petname journal loading fails on invalid complete records; the journal format and torn-tail behavior are unchanged.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/9007/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/9007/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}